We need to show Ipilimumab combination trials in Melanoma with sample sizes. So we need rows where "name_of_ici" (or "name_of_ici_1") includes Ipilimumab, and "cancer_type" includes Melanoma, and likely "monotherapy_combination" indicates combination? Could also use "type_of_combination" or "type_of_combination_1". But we can filter by "name_of_ici" ILIKE '%Ipilimumab%' and "cancer_type" ILIKE '%Melanoma%'. Also need sample sizes: column "total_sample_size". The requirement: unless question asks for count, return rows and always include "nct","author","year","pubmed_id". Also include sample size column. So we need to include "total_sample_size". Also maybe include "treatment_regimen" etc but not required. We'll include the required columns plus "total_sample_size". The query: SELECT "nct","author","year","pubmed_id","total_sample_size" FROM public."clinical_trials" WHERE "name_of_ici" ILIKE '%Ipilimumab%' AND "cancer_type" ILIKE '%Melanoma%' AND "monotherapy_combination" ILIKE '%combination%';